{"id": "EUVD-2026-92135", "enisaUuid": "9c82079f-fb4a-3720-9230-98efc9952aba", "description": "The alexpechkarev/google-maps Laravel package through 12.16 disables TLS certificate verification by default because the bundled config sets ssl_verify_peer to FALSE, which is passed to CURLOPT_SSL_VERIFYPEER. On-path attackers can present any certificate to intercept Google Maps web-service requests, steal the API key from the query string, and tamper with responses.", "datePublished": "2026-10-04T22:31:47", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-05T13:19:20", "baseScore": 9.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/alexpechkarev/google-maps/issues/123", "https://github.com/alexpechkarev/google-maps", "https://github.com/alexpechkarev/google-maps/blob/v12.16/src/config/googlemaps.php#L28", "https://github.com/alexpechkarev/google-maps/blob/v12.14/src/WebService.php#L267-L269", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/alexpechkarev-google-maps-through-12.16-disabled-tls-certificate-verification-via-ssl-verify-peer"], "aliases": ["GHSA-mpgp-p4pg-fp7c", "CVE-2026-105222"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.19, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1b7ff986-8e0f-3afa-8e3b-dbe528ea6cee", "product": {"name": "google-maps", "vendor": {"name": "alexpechkarev"}}, "product_version": "1.0.3 \u226412.16"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "7b9e458a-83fa-33b3-840f-f10b4c238422", "vendor": {"name": "alexpechkarev"}}], "isExploited": false}